.TH "RTCPEERCONNECTION.IDPLOGINURL" "3JS" "April 13, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCPeerConnection.idpLoginUrl \- RTCPeerConnection: idpLoginUrl property
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]idpLoginUrl\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]RTCPeerConnection\f[R] interface returns a string containing the
URL endpoint the application can open to log users in to the identity
provider (IdP).
This value is \f[CR]null\f[R] until the IdP indicates that login is
needed.
.PP
When a call to \f[CR]RTCPeerConnection.getIdentityAssertion()\f[R] fails
because the IdP requires user authentication, the resulting promise is
rejected with an \f[CR]RTCError\f[R] whose \f[CR]errorDetail\f[R] is
\f[CR]\(dqidp\-need\-login\(dq\f[R].
The browser then sets this property to the login URL provided by the
IdP.
The application can open this URL (for example, in a pop\-up window or
\f[CR]<iframe>\f[R]) to allow the user to complete the login process
before retrying the identity assertion.
.SH VALUE
A string containing the IdP login URL, or \f[CR]null\f[R] if no login is
needed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Handling an IdP login requirement
In this example, the application attempts to gather an identity
assertion.
If the IdP rejects the attempt because the user is not authenticated,
the application opens the login URL provided in \f[CR]idpLoginUrl\f[R].
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] pc = \f[B]new\f[R] RTCPeerConnection();
pc.setIdentityProvider(\(dqlogin.example.com\(dq);

pc.getIdentityAssertion().catch((error) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]if\f[R] (pc.idpLoginUrl) {
    console.log(\(gaIdP login required at: ${pc.idpLoginUrl}\(ga);
    \f[I]// Open the login page in a popup window\f[R]
    \f[B]const\f[R] loginWindow = window.open(
      pc.idpLoginUrl,
      \(dqidp\-login\(dq,
      \(dqwidth=500,height=600\(dq,
    );
  } \f[B]else\f[R] {
    console.error(\(dqIdentity assertion failed:\(dq, error);
  }
});
.EE
